;; /workflow (RFC-076): keep this project's workflows (.brainyard/deps.edn's
;; :workflows) through agent$workflow. A turn, as every command that stands
;; for an agent is (RFC-004): the session's agent asks agent$workflow, reads
;; its report, and says it.
;;
;; `/workflow` alone lists them; `/workflow WORDS` says what to do with one,
;; or runs one: `/workflow run fix byj-abc`, `/workflow run feature the login
;; page`.
;;
;; Not in brainyard, which has no workflows of stages and roles.
{:command "/workflow"
 :agent "workflow"
 :rephrase :predictor

 :default-request
 "List this project's workflows."

 :purpose
 "keep and run this project's workflows (.brainyard/deps.edn's :workflows: stages, each playing a role, and what one hands the next) — list them, show one, add, change or remove one, each change shown to the person and written only on their yes, or run one on a piece of work, each stage a turn of its own judged by the workflow's master"

 :usage
 "Call agent$workflow with :question set to the request, in the person's words — which workflow to run and on what, when they ask for a run — and read its report. Do not change .brainyard/deps.edn yourself around it, and do not work a run's stages yourself. When it stopped on a question for the person, end with that question as it put it. End with its report as it said it."

 :template
 "{request}

[{command}] This is {command}: {purpose}. {usage}"}
